<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The Halo 3 dialog (Menu style Halo 3): every message box and question the game shows, in one
look - a title, the text, up to three choices in rows, the buttons in a strip at the bottom
(Cross Select, Circle Back: the icons the button icons setting shows), over what is behind,
dimmed. The art is this folder's own (tools/halo3_menu_art.py: dim, panel, rule, strip,
item, the glyphs), the words the port's own (menu_functions.c "port h3 dialog" gives each
its title and text, in the player's language).

The screens stand for the Xbox's message boxes (ui\shell\error\...) while Menu style is
Halo 3, through dialog_ui.xml (the main menu's: ui.map) and dialog_ingame.xml (a level's):
their handlers are the Xbox's (HALO_MENUS_DUMP), so each does what the box it stands for did.
With Menu style Halo CE the Xbox's own boxes open, as ever.

- error, notice (its non-modal one: it closes by itself), half_error, half_notice (split
  screen): display_error's box - its first child's first child is the text box the game
  gives the error's number (ui_widget.c display_error), which "port h3 dialog" reads.
- abort, abort_final: the errors that end the game (display_error_abort_to_dashboard: the
  screen is the text box); exit: "Quitting", then the game ends.
- revert, restart (and half_revert, half_restart, half_quit): the pause screen's questions.
- savequit, saved: SAVE AND QUIT's "Saving", then the main menu.
- saving, creating: the main menu's "Saving" boxes (a profile, a game type).
- delprof, delgt: delete a profile, a game type (the Xbox screens' questions).
- message, question: the port's own (map sharing, invites, the crossplay check, Forge),
  which the platform's own box shows otherwise (menu_functions.c h3_dialog_port). -->
